<title>SOUTH KOREA: Jinro Ltd net rises in year to Sept.</title>
<headline>Jinro Ltd net rises in year to Sept.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to September 31</p>
<p>(in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)				 1,395  vs    1,837</p>
<p>    Net					 16.87  vs    15.82</p>
<p>    Turnover				 436.70  vs   411.66</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries (both loss)	  0.77  vs     2.50</p>
<p>    Profit before tax		     28.74  vs    27.94</p>
<p>NOTE - Jinro Ltd is South Korea's largest maker of soju, a traditional alcoholic drink. A company spokesman said its earnings per share fell during the period due to an increase in share capital. Its share capital increased to 14.12 million shares at the end of September 1996 from 9.62 million a year earlier, due to conversion of convertible bonds and rights and bonus issues, he said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
